  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Land Rights Now campaign</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The **International Land Coalition (ILC)** is a global alliance of over 300 member organizations from 84 countries, including civilsociety and intergovernmental organizations. The ILC&apos;s mission is to promote people-centered land governance, ensuring that land rights are secure and equitable for those who live on and from the land, such as farmers, pastoralists, Indigenous Peoples, women, andyouth. By focusing on sustainable and equitable land use, the ILC aims to build democracy, justice, sustainability, and resilience in communities worldwide

The **Land Rights Now** campaign is closely connected to the ILC&apos;s mission. Launched in 2016 by the ILC, Oxfam, and the Rights and Resources Initiative, this campaign is a global call to action to secure Indigenous and community land rights. It mobilizes citizens, media, communities, and organizations worldwide to advocate for the recognition and protection of these rights. The campaign&apos;s goal is to double the global area of land legally recognized as owned byIndigenous Peoples and local communities.</narrative>
  </description>
